    module: 3,
    title: "Vinca neurotoxicity, ileus, oxaliplatin cold symptoms",
    safetyLevel: "critical",
    body: "**WRONG ROUTE OR OVERDOSE:** [Vinca given intrathecally](#/node/odse-vinca-intrathecal) | [Vinca IV overdose](#/node/odse-vinca-overdose)\n\n**PRESENTATION AND RED FLAGS**\n\u2022 **Vincristine label:** dose-related neurotoxicity: neuritic pain, constipation, sensory loss, paresthesia, difficulty walking, slapping gait, loss of deep-tendon reflexes, muscle wasting; progressive sensorimotor dysfunction with continued treatment. Vinblastine label: neurologic toxicity can be disabling. [52][53]\n\u2022 Ileus: the vincristine overdose text includes enemas or cathartics to prevent ileus, with GI decompression sometimes necessary. [52]\n\u2022 Rare SIADH with vincristine: hyponatremia and high urinary sodium without renal or adrenal disease, hypotension, dehydration, azotemia or edema; improves with fluid deprivation. [52] Navigation: [Sodium consult](#/tree/sodium).\n\u2022 **Oxaliplatin cold-triggered symptoms (label):** transient paresthesia, dysesthesia, hypoesthesia of hands, feet, perioral area or throat; jaw spasm, abnormal tongue sensation, dysarthria, eye pain, chest pressure; about 56% of patients. Pharyngolaryngeal dysesthesia versus anaphylaxis: [Hypersensitivity page](#/node/odse-tox-chemo-hypersensitivity). [42]\n\n**TIMING**\n\u2022 Vincristine: constipation usually <7 days with weekly doses. [52]\n\u2022 Oxaliplatin: onset within hours or 2 days of a dose, resolves within 14 days, recurs with dosing; about 30% in any one cycle. [42]\n\u2022 Cisplatin label: dose-related neuropathy, can begin after one dose; delayed onset 3 to 8 weeks after the last dose. [49]\n\n**WORKUP**\n\u2022 No workup is stated in the sources reviewed.\n\n**TREATMENT**\n\u2022 Oxaliplatin label: reduce the dose or permanently discontinue for persistent neurosensory reactions, by severity. Treatment of the cold-triggered symptoms is not stated in the label text reviewed. [41][42]\n\u2022 Vincristine ileus and neuropathy: no management beyond the overdose text is stated. No guideline was reviewed.\n\n**DO NOT**\n\u2022 Oxaliplatin: avoid ice (including for mucositis prophylaxis) because cold exacerbates acute neurological symptoms; patients advised to avoid cold drinks, ice and cold objects. [42]\n\u2022 Vincristine label: not for patients with demyelinating Charcot-Marie-Tooth; avoid strong CYP3A inhibitors (itraconazole or fluconazole reported to cause earlier onset and/or more severe neuromuscular effects). [52]\n\n**DISPOSITION**\n\u2022 Not stated in the sources reviewed.\n\u2022 **Clinical note (myMedKitt editor, not from the cited sources):** disposition is decided with the treating oncologist.",
    options: [{"label": "Vinca alkaloid given intrathecally (wrong route)", "next": "odse-vinca-intrathecal", "urgency": "critical"}, {"label": "Vinca alkaloid overdose (IV)", "next": "odse-vinca-overdose"}],
