    body: "\u2022 Electrolyte disturbance is a recognised adverse effect of the drug classes on the cards that carry it: BCR-ABL tyrosine kinase inhibitors (nilotinib); VEGFR-targeting kinase inhibitors (cabozantinib, lenvatinib mesylate); FGFR kinase inhibitors (erdafitinib, pemigatinib, futibatinib); Estrogen receptor antagonists (tamoxifen citrate); Aromatase inhibitors (anastrozole); Androgen synthesis inhibitor (CYP17) (abiraterone acetate); GnRH agonists (goserelin); Anti-EGFR antibodies (cetuximab, panitumumab, necitumumab); Anti-GD2 antibodies (dinutuximab); Interleukin-2 lymphocyte growth factor (aldesleukin); CD22-directed cytotoxin (moxetumomab pasudotox-tdfk).\n\u2022 The drug's own label instruction (withhold, permanently discontinue, named rescue agent, monitoring threshold), where the label gives one, is on the drug's card under this effect.\n\n**Related consults (differential, overlap and supportive care; the drug's label instruction is on its card):**\n\u2022 [Magnesium Disorders](#/tree/magnesium-disorders/node/mg-start)\n\u2022 [Calcium Disorders](#/tree/calcium-disorders/node/ca-start)\n\u2022 [Hypokalemia assessment (Potassium Disorders)](#/tree/potassium/node/k-hypo-assess)\n\u2022 [Phosphorous Disorders](#/tree/phosphorus-disorders/node/phos-start)\n\u2022 [Sodium Disorders](#/tree/sodium/node/na-start)\n\u2022 [Hypercalcemia of malignancy (Oncological Emergencies)](#/tree/oncological-emergencies/node/onc-hyperca-recognize)\n\n**Not covered:** The app has no consult specific to drug-induced electrolyte disturbance; the consults above are organized by electrolyte.\n\n**Clinical note (myMedKitt editor, not from the cited sources):** disposition is decided with the treating oncologist.",
