    body: "\u2022 Kidney toxicity is a recognised adverse effect of the drug classes on the cards that carry it: BCR-ABL tyrosine kinase inhibitors (imatinib mesylate, dasatinib, bosutinib); Janus kinase (JAK) inhibitors for myelofibrosis (pacritinib); Proteasome inhibitors (carfilzomib); EGFR tyrosine kinase inhibitor (erlotinib); ALK or ROS1 kinase inhibitor (alectinib hydrochloride); KRAS G12C inhibitor (adagrasib); BRAF kinase inhibitor (vemurafenib); VEGFR-targeting kinase inhibitors (lenvatinib mesylate, vandetanib); mTOR inhibitors (everolimus, temsirolimus); Anti-CD20 antibodies (rituximab); Anti-HER2 antibodies (trastuzumab); Drugs that block the VEGF pathway (bevacizumab, ramucirumab, ziv-aflibercept); Anti-EGFR antibodies (panitumumab); Tumor-derived autologous T cell immunotherapy (lifileucel); Interleukin-2 lymphocyte growth factor (aldesleukin); CD22-directed cytotoxin (moxetumomab pasudotox-tdfk).\n\u2022 The drug's own label instruction (withhold, permanently discontinue, named rescue agent, monitoring threshold), where the label gives one, is on the drug's card under this effect.\n\n**Related consults (differential, overlap and supportive care; the drug's label instruction is on its card):**\n\u2022 [Potassium Disorders](#/tree/potassium/node/k-start): electrolytes\n\u2022 [Magnesium Disorders](#/tree/magnesium-disorders/node/mg-start): electrolytes\n\u2022 [Tumor lysis syndrome (Oncological Emergencies)](#/tree/oncological-emergencies/node/onc-tls-recognize): differential\n\u2022 [Rhabdomyolysis](#/tree/rhabdomyolysis/node/rhabdo-start): differential\n\u2022 [Thrombotic Thrombocytopenic Purpura (TTP)](#/tree/ttp/node/ttp-start): differential: thrombotic microangiopathy\n\n**Not covered:** The app has no acute kidney injury consult.\n\n**Clinical note (myMedKitt editor, not from the cited sources):** disposition is decided with the treating oncologist.",
    summary: "Label instruction on the drug card where given; related consults (differential, overlap, supportive care): Potassium Disorders, Magnesium Disorders, Tumor lysis syndrome, Rhabdomyolysis, Thrombotic Thrombocytopenic Purpura (TTP)",
